WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.380
The decay constant tells you how likely
a nucleus is to decay in a short time.

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:09.390
So for a longer time, why not
just multiply it by the time?

3
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.500
Wait long enough, and
that product reaches 2.

4
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:16.950
Read as a probability, that's a
200 per cent chance of decaying.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.270
Can a nucleus ever be more
than certain to decay?

6
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.450
In this mission, you'll find out what
the decay constant really measures.

7
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.940
Then you'll pit the shortcut
against the exact probability,

8
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.520
and test both on one half-life.

9
00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:35.240
Your mission: find out whether a chance
of decay can ever pass certainty.
